Do not steal focus for override-redirect popups on first configure.

Steam's menu bar dropdowns (Steam, View, Friends, Games, Help) open and dismiss
themselves within ~35ms under niri, so they cannot be navigated at all. The
menus never reach niri as windows: a `niri msg event-stream` capture during a
click shows no window open or close events, which places the fault in
xwayland-satellite's handling of the X11 override-redirect surface rather than
in any niri window rule.

Upstream bisected this to 3273a0fccd71da21c6362c74f3b1d1c0a89ff3ba ("Fix: unity
editor add component pop up", #397), which landed after v0.8.1 and shipped in
v0.8.2. It focuses the popup as soon as the compositor configures it. Steam
holds an X11 grab on its main window, so that focus change makes Steam revert
`_NET_ACTIVE_WINDOW` to the main window a moment later and the menu tears down.
A follow-up, 5d1efbc9 ("server: only focus 'passive' popups"), narrowed the
condition to `require_wm_focus()` but Steam still trips it.

This drops the focus block, restoring the v0.8.1 behaviour while keeping the
rest of v0.8.2 (the output scale and geometry fixes matter on a multi-monitor
setup). The `first_configure` binding goes with it since nothing else reads it.
`FocusData` stays imported; it is still used by the keyboard focus path.

The cost is reverting #397, so the Unity editor's "Add Component" search bar
loses its input fix. Nothing here uses the Unity editor.

Tracked upstream as https://github.com/Supreeeme/xwayland-satellite/issues/468,
still open. Drop this patch once that is fixed and released.

Recheck against src/server/event.rs on every xwayland-satellite bump.

